libapache2-mod-maat (0.20.0~alpha3-1) unstable; urgency=low

  * Add isolated Ed25519 issuer-mediated, service-scoped 5-minute credentials.
  * Require citizen-key possession, default-deny anonymous rights and one-use proofs.
  * Pin issuer/HMAC anchors to keep nullifiers stable across key renewals and bans.
  * Not zero-knowledge anonymous; issuer sees citizen and scope, no live SSH bridge trust.

 -- Maât contributors <maat-developers@localhost>  Fri, 16 Oct 2026 15:00:00 +0200

libapache2-mod-maat (0.20.0~alpha2-1) unstable; urgency=low

  * Authenticate administrative registry commands using pinned Ed25519 authority.
  * Add persistent counter/registry-domain replay protection and transactional audit.
  * Preserve fail-closed anonymous-default policy; no anonymous proofs enabled.
  * Still an integration prototype; Docker/QEMU alpha2 tests not yet run.

 -- Maât contributors <maat-developers@localhost>  Fri, 16 Oct 2026 13:00:00 +0200

libapache2-mod-maat (0.20.0~alpha1-1) unstable; urgency=low

  * Begin administrative citizen registry with unique subject commitments.
  * Add default-deny anonymous permissions and durable scoped ban ledger.
  * No anonymous credentials or civil identity verification enabled.
  * Non-production prototype; integration tests pending for this alpha.

 -- Maât contributors <maat-developers@localhost>  Fri, 16 Oct 2026 11:00:00 +0200

libapache2-mod-maat (0.19.0~rc1-1) unstable; urgency=low

  * Validate SSH-bound PHP request identity in Docker and independent QEMU E2E.
  * Add bounded reusable SSH session capacity, fresh TCP proof per HTTP request.
  * Support pipelined and sequential HTTP/1.1 with strict framing.
  * Harden SQLite contention and adversarial integration tests.
  * Not approved for public production, services stay disabled by default.

 -- Maât contributors <maat-developers@localhost>  Tue, 13 Oct 2026 17:30:00 +0200

libapache2-mod-maat (0.18.0-1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Bind Apache requests to SSH-authenticated live TCP descriptors via broker.
  * Remove bearer tickets from the HTTP transport and PHP application layer.
  * Reject unmatched requests on the dedicated Maât listener.

 -- Maât contributors <maat-developers@localhost>  Tue, 13 Oct 2026 12:00:00 +0200

libapache2-mod-maat (0.17.0-1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Make direct broker verification the sole private-ingress mode.
  * Remove legacy MaatDirectVerify switch and PHP bearer revalidation.
  * Expose only request-scoped verified identity via Apache optional function.

 -- Maât contributors <maat-developers@localhost>  Tue, 13 Oct 2026 08:00:00 +0200

libapache2-mod-maat (0.16.0-1) unstable; urgency=low

  * Add opt-in broker verification within Apache request hook.
  * Provide request-local optional native API; fail closed without broker.
  * Keep the old PHP ticket path as the default and require explicit opt-in.
  * Direct mode is experimental and is not enabled by packaging.

 -- Maât contributors <maat-developers@localhost>  Mon, 12 Oct 2026 22:00:00 +0200

libapache2-mod-maat (0.15.0-1) unstable; urgency=low

  * Add experimental opt-in Apache 2.4 Maât ingress filter.
  * Reject spoofable or malformed identity headers by default.
  * This package does not enable the module automatically.

